1a99|n|Mass; church service. ; A quantity of food set on a table at one time; provision of food for a person or party for one meal; as, a mess of pottage; also, the food given to a beast at one time. ; A number of persons who eat together, and for whom food is prepared in common; especially, persons in the military or naval service who eat at the same table; as, the wardroom mess. ; A set of four; -- from the old practice of dividing companies into sets of four at dinner. ; The milk given by a cow at one milking. ; A disagreeable mixture or confusion of things; hence, a situation resulting from blundering or from misunderstanding; as, he made a mess of it.	a:xc2,97,1;206v,85,5;28io,79,1;zb9,65,2;7sf,45,8;eld,43,4;zdz,35,6;1pse,27,2~7sf,45,8;zdz,35,6;206v,85,5;eld,43,4;1pse,27,2;zb9,65,2;28io,79,1;xc2,97,1	n:28io,89,2;zdz,9,1~28io,89,2;zdz,9,1	N:3tv,26,4~3tv,26,4
